 kit flow - shows where the work stands, from the issues to releases

   one of
   *kit flow*                   shows where the work stands, from the issues to releases

     --no-fetch   --fresh     fetches nothing; incoming says so

     --text   --json   --jq   prints the picture as text, even on a terminal

     one of
     --all                    every issue and pull request (the default); it stands alone
     --mine --others --owner

   --stages                   prints the stages the picture draws, one per line, in order
   --me                       prints the caller's login on the primary's forge, the login --mine and
                              --others match
   --capabilities             prints what the primary's forge can do, as one JSON object: {contract,
                              forge, provider, features}, each feature native or none, as
                              modules/bash/forge.sh declares them; it asks nothing
   --quota                    prints the caller's rate limits on the primary's forge, as one JSON
                              array: each forge's {forge, limits}, each limit {name, limit,
                              remaining, reset}; reading them costs a request at most. A forge
                              without rate limits gives none, and asks nothing
   --marks                    prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what
                              the stage draws does: read again, a mark that differs says the stage
                              is stale; on GitHub, nothing changed costs no request
   issues                     every open issue, oldest first: in the backlog, which no open pull
                              request closes, or underway, closed by one: who works on each, and
                              where
   incoming                   what fetching every remote brought: default-branch commits, branches
                              new and gone
   changes                    the open pull requests, each with the issues it closes
   builds                     the runs not owned by any pull request: the default branch, tags,
                              schedules
   releases                   the releases on the forge, newest first
   desk                       no stage of kit flow: kit workspace worktrees draws the root checkout,
                              its first row
   worktrees                  no stage of kit flow: kit workspace worktrees draws the linked
                              worktrees
   backlog                    no stage of kit flow: issues lists them; on a terminal it opens issues
                              on its Backlog preset
   underway                   no stage of kit flow: issues lists them; on a terminal it opens issues
                              on its Underway preset


 kit flow
